### What this track proposes
This chore makes the jr-green role gate ignore at most one open `[~]` task whose title starts with a later-role label. A case-insensitive regex pins the labels `Review A`, `Review B`, `Review C`, `Adversarial`, and `Acceptance`, and a word in the body never matches. A helper used only by the jr-green branch holds the logic, and `phase_counts` keeps its five-value return. A `[ ]` task, a `deferred` task, a second label task, and the SHA-evidence check stay as today. Red adds a contract test with named fixtures, Green adds the helper, and the change set holds one `CHANGELOG.md` entry.

### How the current system works, per this spec
`phase_counts` in `skills/measure-orchestrator/scripts/measure_interphase_checks.py` reads one phase of `plan.md` and returns five counts. A task counts as incomplete when it is not `[x]` and its text has no `deferred`. The jr-green branch fails with `current phase still has N non-deferred incomplete tasks` when the incomplete count is above zero. Mid-red, jr-green, and the review and phase-acceptance branch each unpack the five values, and final-acceptance uses `track_incomplete`. Lending rule A12 marks the review task `[~]` before Review A starts, so the open task 3.5 fails the jr-green gate.

### Findings
- F7 [Nit] spec.md FR-1: The number part of the regex, `\d+(?:\.\d+)*`, accepts no letter, so `- [~] 4b.5 Review A.` and `- [~] 4.13s Adversarial tests` still fail the jr-green gate. Rationale: The regex matches 13 of 15 distinct role tasks in the Measure and Lending plans. It misses `4b.5` (daily_model_schedule) and `4.13s` (model_guide). The miss is safe, because the gate fails as today. Allow one letter after each number. Add one Red case.
- F8 [Nit] plan.md Task 1.2: FR-4 adds one `CHANGELOG.md` entry, but no task owns it. Task 1.2 cites FR-1 through FR-3, and Task 1.3 holds only the pull request and the records. Add the entry to Task 1.2. Rationale: The four earlier checker commits (f68a87f, 94698fe, 7e6dc79, 27c2ed0) each added the entry with the checker change. The Green role file names implementation files, Green tests, and plan updates, not `CHANGELOG.md`. A task without an owner can leave FR-4 open until phase acceptance.
- F9 [Nit] spec.md FR-4: FR-4 says `exactly`, but the closeout step of the light lane changes more files. Name them again: `measure/tracks.md`, `measure/archive/<track>/`, and `measure/runs/<track>/`. Rationale: The earlier text of FR-4 named the closeout files, and the revision removed that sentence. The closeout of audit_role_gate_allow_20261123 (commit 800df77) changed all three paths. An auditor can read `exactly` as a scope breach.

