OBSERVATIONS (not findings)
1. Task 1.3 stays open at the Green gate. The jr-green gate exits 1 after Task 1.2 until a records round closes Task 1.3. The precedent audit_role_gate_allow_20261123 gave the same result.
2. The mid-red expected output reads "identical before and after". The literal is `PASS: mid-red gate passed`, and the implementer reads it from the current checker. No decision is open.
3. The group `(?:\s+testing)?` in the regex never changes a match, because `\b` already accepts `adversarial` before a space. It is harmless.
4. A closed [x] review task plus a [~] Green fix task is the Lending fix-round shape (model_guide tasks 4.13i to 4.13x). The natural helper filters on `[~]`, and the [ ] case catches a helper with no filter. One more Red case would pin it. This is optional.
5. The near-miss fixtures reuse task ids (`Task 1.2` twice in near-miss 1, `Task 3.5` in a Phase 1 fixture). The checker ignores ids, so the reuse has no effect.
6. The line numbers in FR-3 are the numbers at HEAD c5bc2ff. They shift after Green.
7. A work task whose title starts with `Acceptance` or `Adversarial` would use the one ignore. The corpus holds no such task. The risk is low and the trade-off is sound.
8. The Measure plans word review tasks as `Task N.M: Run measure-review-a-correctness ...`. The rule leaves such a title open. The scope is Lending rule A12, so this is safe and in scope.
9. Environment: the edit rule denied a script file in /tmp, so all experiments ran from stdin. The shell rule `*rm *` denied two runs because a variable name ended in `rm`. This is the known unanchored-glob issue.

VERDICT
Pass. No Blocker and no Major remain. Three Nits (F7, F8, F9) remain, and the standard accepts open Nits after this round.
